                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "Using Sources Effectively",
            "block_bbox": [
                80,
                345,
                401,
                377
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 5,
            "group_id": 6,
            "global_block_id": 6,
            "global_group_id": 6,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    80.0,
                    345.0
                ],
                [
                    401.0,
                    345.0
                ],
                [
                    401.0,
                    377.0
                ],
                [
                    80.0,
                    377.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Again, to use sources ethically, you must quote accurately, paraphrase appropriately, and follow the citation conventions of your field. But to use sources effectively, you must do more than follow sound rules and practices. As with other aspects of style, you have choices in how you incorporate sources into your writing, and you can shape the responses of your readers through the choices you make. To use a source in your writing, you have to make at least three decisions:",
            "block_bbox": [
                78,
                390,
                773,
                569
            ],
            "block_id": 7,
            "block_order": 6,
            "group_id": 7,
            "global_block_id": 7,
            "global_group_id": 7,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    78.0,
                    390.0
                ],
                [
                    773.0,
                    390.0
                ],
                [
                    773.0,
                    569.0
                ],
                [
                    78.0,
                    569.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "- How much of the source to include: Will you use just a word or phrase, a sentence, a passage, or a summary of the whole?",
            "block_bbox": [
                103,
                582,
                771,
                633
            ],
            "block_id": 8,
            "block_order": 7,
            "group_id": 8,
            "global_block_id": 8,
            "global_group_id": 8,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    103.0,
                    582.0
                ],
                [
                    771.0,
                    582.0
                ],
                [
                    771.0,
                    633.0
                ],
                [
                    103.0,
                    633.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "- How to include it: Will you use the source's exact words or put its ideas into your own words?",
            "block_bbox": [
                103,
                641,
                740,
                691
            ],
            "block_id": 9,
            "block_order": 8,
            "group_id": 9,
            "global_block_id": 9,
            "global_group_id": 9,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    103.0,
                    641.0
                ],
                [
                    740.0,
                    641.0
                ],
                [
                    740.0,
                    691.0
                ],
                [
                    103.0,
                    691.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "- How to attribute it: Will you explicitly attribute the words or ideas you use to the source's author?",
            "block_bbox": [
                102,
                699,
                771,
                748
            ],
            "block_id": 10,
            "block_order": 9,
            "group_id": 10,
            "global_block_id": 10,
            "global_group_id": 10,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    102.0,
                    699.0
                ],
                [
                    771.0,
                    699.0
                ],
                [
                    771.0,
                    748.0
                ],
                [
                    102.0,
                    748.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Before we discuss these choices, a word of caution: like citation conventions, ways of using sources vary from field to field. In some fields, writers quote extensively; in others, they quote rarely, relying instead on summary and paraphrase. The best way to learn the typical practices of your field is to read writers who are recognized authorities in it.",
            "block_bbox": [
                78,
                763,
                772,
                890
            ],
            "block_id": 11,
            "block_order": 10,
            "group_id": 11,
            "global_block_id": 11,
            "global_group_id": 11,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    78.0,
                    763.0
                ],
                [
                    772.0,
                    763.0
                ],
                [
                    772.0,
                    890.0
                ],
                [
                    78.0,
                    890.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Here, in general terms, are your options. (Note: these illustrations use parenthetical citations; in your own writing, you should follow the conventions of your field.)",
            "block_bbox": [
                78,
                893,
                771,
                944
            ],
            "block_id": 12,
            "block_order": 11,
            "group_id": 12,
            "global_block_id": 12,
            "global_group_id": 12,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    78.0,
                    893.0
                ],
                [
                    771.0,
                    893.0
                ],
                [
                    771.0,
                    944.0
                ],
                [
                    78.0,
                    944.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "How Much of a Source to Include?",
            "block_bbox": [
                80,
                962,
                454,
                987
            ],
            "block_id": 13,
            "block_order": 12,
            "group_id": 13,
            "global_block_id": 13,
            "global_group_id": 13,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    80.0,
                    962.0
                ],
                [
                    454.0,
                    962.0
                ],
                [
                    454.0,
                    987.0
                ],
                [
                    80.0,
                    987.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "To use a source in your writing, you must first decide how much of it to include through quotation, paraphrase, or summary: just a few words, a single sentence, a longer passage, a summary of the whole? There are no hard-and-fast rules that answer this question, but here are three principles to help you choose:",
            "block_bbox": [
                79,
                997,
                772,
                1100
            ],
            "block_id": 14,
            "block_order": 13,
            "group_id": 14,
            "global_block_id": 14,
            "global_group_id": 14,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    79.0,
                    997.0
                ],
                [
                    772.0,
                    997.0
                ],
                [
                    772.0,
                    1100.0
                ],
                [
                    79.0,
                    1100.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "1. Include just as much of a source as you need. If you don't quote or paraphrase enough, your writing can seem thin and disconnected from the larger conversation to which it contributes; if you quote or paraphrase too much, your writing can seem plodding or insecure. It's hard to know what's \"just right\": that sense of proportion comes gradually, through instruction, reading,",
            "block_bbox": [
                80,
                1113,
                772,
                1244
            ],
            "block_id": 15,
            "block_order": 14,
            "group_id": 15,
            "global_block_id": 15,
            "global_group_id": 15,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    80.0,
                    1113.0
                ],
                [
                    772.0,
                    1113.0
                ],
